  + [status] is raw_preserved_unprocessed

& [Problem] is a representation gap before M2C
  + current formation defines two distinct actual complete acquisition lineages, causal order, common scope, independent carriers, and Equal reconciliation
  + current production code has no bounded type for acquisition identity, scope, lineage, order, evidence derivation input, or derivation fault
  + direct Windows scanner code would otherwise invent those data contracts and authority boundaries while implementing effects
  + current TopologyReceipt carries only an evidence-grade label and cannot carry or prove its support lineage
  + current supplied carriers retain pure derivation ancestry but cannot identify physical origin
  + public serde values are inspectable but caller construction cannot establish actual acquisition
  + opaque production records can restrict construction but may hide evidence needed for inspection, serialization, and review

& [Purpose] is define pure inspectable claims without self-authorizing provenance
  + create strict bounded forms for acquisition identity, scope, lineage claims, exact ordered pair claims, derivation plans, results, and faults
  + reuse current topology forms, inventory assembly carriers, ordered digest carriers, reconciliation plan and result, and InventoryConsistencyEvidence meanings by reference
  + make every form validation rule pure
  + distinguish a well-formed claim from production-admitted acquisition provenance
  + require later M2C source to bind construction authority to actual successful observation
  + prevent pure forms or test fixtures from being cited as physical evidence

& [PrimaryDelineation] is mandatory
  + ClaimForm is caller-constructible inspectable data
  + ValidClaim is a pure structural and relational validation result
  + ProductionConstructionAuthority is a later capability owned by an authorized physical producer
  + AdmittedAcquisitionLineage is a later output that combines valid claim with production provenance
  + EvidenceDerivationClaim is a pure representation of the required conjunction
  + IssuedEvidence is a later authority-bearing result
  + TopologyReceipt issuance and consumption remain later distinct stages
  + no selected pure form crosses these boundaries by itself

& [AcquisitionIdentity] is role specific
  + identity names one claimed acquisition event
  + identity is distinct from scan nonce, correlation UUID, candidate root, path, file identity, inventory digest, receipt hash, ordinal, tick, or operand index
  + exact representation must be bounded, canonical, nonempty, and round-trip stable
  + identity uniqueness cannot be proven by syntax alone
  + two-role validation requires exact inequality
  + generation is not performed by this slice
  + SJS must decide whether representation reuses an existing bounded identity primitive or introduces one exact wrapper without randomness or clock use

& [AcquisitionScopeClaim] is a complete product
  + candidate root reference
  + strong root identity
  + canonical root volume-GUID path
  + scanner profile cantor-windows-candidate-topology/0.1
  + current machine forms profile
  + current topology forms profile
  + current topology receipt profile where receipt relation is claimed
  + current ordered observation encoding profile
  + complete TopologyScanLimits value
  + closed policy digest
  + predecessor admission profile and receipt digest
  + comparison scope identity
  + every coordinate is required and validated using current forms
  + no missing coordinate, optional wildcard, default, or partial comparison exists

& [AcquisitionLineageClaim] represents one claimed complete event
  + exact acquisition identity
  + exact acquisition scope claim
  + exact acquisition role is not stored as first or second inside the lineage
  + exact current supplied topology inventory assembly carrier or stable reference to its complete lineage
  + exact current ordered topology inventory digest carrier or stable reference to its complete lineage
  + explicit completion disposition from a closed claim vocabulary
  + completion claim does not prove physical traversal occurred
  + lineage validation reruns every current pure carrier validation and derivation that remains available
  + bare digest input is forbidden

& [CompletionDisposition] is closed and non-authorizing
  + CompleteClaimed means the form claims its acquisition completed under the exact scope
  + IncompleteClaimed or FaultedClaimed may be represented only if a consumer need is established during SJS
  + a successful evidence derivation input requires CompleteClaimed for both lineages
  + no disposition token is named Observed, Proven, Actual, Trusted, Admitted, or Issued
  + SJS must prune unneeded variants rather than model speculative runtime lifecycle

& [OrderedAcquisitionPairClaim] is exact
  + owns or references exactly two complete AcquisitionLineageClaim values
  + maps them explicitly to FirstAcquisition and SecondAcquisition roles
  + requires distinct acquisition identities
  + requires exact scope equality
  + represents FirstCompletionStrictlyPrecedesSecondStart as a claimed causal relation
  + causal relation is not inferred from vector order, JSON field order, names, or reconciliation operand positions
  + no numeric clock or tick is required in profile 0.1 unless SJS proves it is necessary and still effect-free

& [CausalOrderClaim] is inspectable and bounded
  + contains exact relation kind FirstCompletionStrictlyPrecedesSecondStart
  + binds both acquisition identities in exact roles
  + contains no wall-clock claim
  + contains no monotonic-clock claim
  + contains no duration or freshness claim
  + pure validation checks role identity, distinctness, and relation coherence only
  + later producer authority must prove the claimed relation from actual control flow or separately governed observations

& [CarrierBinding] preserves complete ancestry
  + one lineage's ordered digest carrier must derive from that same lineage's inventory assembly carrier
  + current validation and canonical derivation are rerun rather than trusting copied digest text
  + reference, profile, encoding, limits, root, policy, and other current carrier fields must match acquisition scope
  + first carrier cannot satisfy second lineage and second cannot satisfy first
  + full output-only carrier types remain the semantic input; no raw assembly, bare digest, or caller summary substitute is accepted

& [RepeatedInventoryEvidencePlan] is pure and exact
  + plan profile is exact 0.1
  + input is one OrderedAcquisitionPairClaim
  + plan binds exact current reconciliation profile and plan
  + plan requests InventoryConsistencyEvidence.NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual only
  + OsSnapshotProven is rejected because no snapshot provenance is represented
  + plan has no issuer, receipt, clock, filesystem, or consumer fields
  + successful plan validation proves only coherent claimed prerequisites

& [RepeatedInventoryEvidenceClaim] is a non-authoritative derivation record
  + retains the complete ordered pair claim
  + retains exact current reconciliation input and result lineage
  + requires current reconciliation disposition Equal
  + names claimed evidence grade NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual
  + explicitly marks provenance grade as ClaimOnly or another exact non-authorizing term selected by SJS
  + cannot convert directly to TopologyReceipt
  + cannot be cited as actual acquisition, issuer proof, admission, or mutation authority

& [ProductionConstructionBoundary] is the central design gate
  + ordinary public decode and validation produce only claim forms
  + production-admitted lineage cannot be created through Deserialize, Default, From, Into, public fields, or unrestricted public constructor
  + later M2C adapter needs a narrow construction path after successful physical observation
  + pure forms slice may define an opaque sealed capability interface or may defer the admitted wrapper entirely
  + SJS must compare private fields, crate-confined constructors, sealed traits, capability tokens, separate claim and admitted record types, and complete deferral
  + selected design must remain testable without making test fixtures indistinguishable from production provenance
  + any test-only construction path is compile-time test-only and carries explicit synthetic provenance
  + no cryptographic key, global registry, process secret, or persistent ledger is assumed without new source

& [SerializationBoundary] is strict
  + claim forms may use serde only when inspectable transport is needed
  + production capability tokens and admitted wrappers are not deserializable from untrusted bytes
  + deny_unknown_fields applies to every serialized struct
  + exact profile fields precede semantic validation
  + no aliases, defaults, flattening, untagged enums, catch-all maps, free strings, or compatibility fallbacks
  + current nested forms retain their exact existing profiles and strict validators

& [ValidationPipeline] is deterministic
  + validate exact profile
  + validate acquisition identity syntax and bounds
  + validate complete scope through current nested forms
  + validate lineage completion claim
  + validate current inventory and digest carrier lineages
  + validate two distinct identities
  + validate exact scope equality
  + validate causal role relation
  + validate current reconciliation plan and independently rederive both carrier results
  + require Equal
  + require selected evidence grade NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual
  + release one complete claim record or one atomic typed fault
  + exact order may change only through canonical SJS decision and direct tests

& [FaultModel] is closed and bounded
  + InvalidRequest for malformed outer request or unsupported capability
  + Profile for exact profile mismatch
  + Identity for malformed, empty, over-bound, duplicate, or role-mismatched acquisition identity
  + Scope for invalid or unequal complete scope
  + Lineage for incomplete, stale, mismatched, bare, or invalid carrier ancestry
  + Order for absent, wrong-role, self, inverse, cyclic, or unsupported causal relation
  + Reconciliation for current validation or derivation fault
  + Different for valid current reconciliation disposition Different
  + Evidence for unsupported evidence grade or self-authorization attempt
  + Capability for attempted production construction without later authorized capability
  + Resource for any declared bound failure
  + no fault contains partial admitted provenance or authoritative receipt

& [OwnershipAndVisibility] require SJS decision
  + public inspectable claim forms own bounded supplied data
  + current output-only carrier ownership remains unchanged
  + validation borrows where possible and returns owned bounded faults
  + admitted production provenance, if formed now, uses opaque ownership and non-forgeable construction within the current crate boundary
  + no global mutable state, thread-local authority, process secret, persistence, database, or cross-process token
  + module visibility must be the narrowest that permits later adapter integration

& [ResourcePolicy] is bounded
  + reuse existing entry, path, stream, file, total, and carrier bounds
  + acquisition identity and comparison-scope representations have explicit byte bounds
  + two lineages only
  + no unbounded vectors, maps, recursion, arbitrary JSON values, free-form diagnostics, or user-selected type tags
  + validation and rederivation share existing bounded complexity
  + new error messages obey existing diagnostic bounds

& [TestRequirements] are adversarial
  + exact positive round trip for every serialized claim form
  + unknown field, wrong profile, malformed and over-bound identity, incomplete scope, and nested-profile rejection
  + duplicate identity, swapped role, self-order, wrong order relation, scope mismatch, carrier mismatch, and bare digest rejection
  + current reconciliation fault and Different remain distinct
  + Equal without production provenance remains ClaimOnly
  + public serde and constructors cannot create an admitted production record
  + test fixture provenance is synthetic and cannot cross the production API
  + OsSnapshotProven, quiescence, stability, current truth, receipt conversion, issuer, and consumer paths remain absent
  + static checks reject unsafe, platform, filesystem, clock, process, network, persistence, model, tool, fixture, and effect imports
  + global debug, overflow-checked release, quality, audit, recursive evidence, provenance, rollback, and clean publication

